From: ODM-conda packaging <packaging@odm-conda.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Write no-normals radius sampling results back to the point list

Upstream commit 6e0c1c0113939823b2ff3c2eef4d5907e7f5db6b (ODM tag 331).

FastSampleFilter::run() copies file.points into a local vector. For point
clouds without normals, the sampling branch erased rejected points from that
local copy only, so the output kept every input point. The branch now builds
the kept list and assigns it to file.points. Without normals, file.extras stays
empty, so it is not touched.

Normals-bearing input follows the unchanged branch, so its output is unchanged.

Status: local packaging patch, not reviewed upstream. Licensing and
corresponding-source review remain open in Backlog TASK-2 and TASK-3.
---
diff --git a/fastsamplefilter.hpp b/fastsamplefilter.hpp
index dda0dc6..95432ee 100644
--- a/fastsamplefilter.hpp
+++ b/fastsamplefilter.hpp
@@ -97,9 +97,23 @@ namespace FPCFilter {
 
             } else {
 
-                auto res = std::remove_if(points.begin(), points.end(), [this](PlyPoint& point) { return !this->safe_voxelize(point); });
-                points.erase(res, points.end());
-                
+                // Write the kept points back: erasing from the local copy alone
+                // leaves file.points unchanged. Without normals, extras stay empty.
+                std::vector<PlyPoint> newPoints;
+                newPoints.reserve(cnt);
+
+                for (std::size_t n = 0; n < cnt; n++) {
+                    const auto& point = points[n];
+
+                    if (this->safe_voxelize(point)) {
+                        newPoints.push_back(point);
+                    }
+                }
+
+                newPoints.shrink_to_fit();
+
+                file.points = newPoints;
+
             }
         }
 
